note Everything xtask does outside itself: starting a program, writing a file, asking the version control system, printing. Each has one function, and the first two are the only places clippy's disallowed methods are expected in xtask (arch.rs EXPECTS), so xtask follows the same one-way rule it enforces on the workspace.

